# Config JSON vs Team YAML

## Two separate configs

| File | Purpose | Module |
|------|---------|--------|
| `config.json` (repo root) | Creo ETL client registry, 340B IDs, domain→client mapping | `app/config_json.py` |
| `config/team.yaml` | Shared team settings, categories, domain hints, tenant | `app/team_config.py` |

## Do not merge

- Client abbrev mapping belongs in `config.json`.
- Category labels and scrape defaults belong in `team.yaml`.
- Studio exposes both via separate API routes.

## Rules

- Update `config/team.yaml.example` when team schema changes.
- Treat `config.json` as business-sensitive data.
- Test client suggest logic in `tests/test_config_json.py`.
